ACADEMIC LINEAGE

This simulation is independent work. Its mechanics draw on published
scholarship, which is unprotectable subject matter under 17 U.S.C. § 102(b);
its narrative, interface, parameters and coursework are original.

Intellectual debts, gratefully acknowledged:

  Ford, D. & Sterman, J. (1998). Dynamic Modeling of Product Development
      Processes. MIT System Dynamics Group D-4672.
  Cooper, K. (1993). The Rework Cycle: Why Projects Are Mismanaged.
  Abdel-Hamid, T. & Madnick, S. (1991). Software Project Dynamics.
      Prentice-Hall.
  Austin, R. D. Project Management Simulation: Scope, Resources, Schedule.
      — prior art in the genre. No material from that commercial product
      was consulted in building this one.

Underlying ideas: Knight (1921) on risk versus uncertainty; Taleb (2007) on
tail risk; Mellers et al. (2015) on calibration as a cultivable skill.
